    "salt": "_Aixeonqfpry93XLbha-OQ==",
    "text": "Oweynagat, the Cave of the Cats, is an Irish mythological site. It lies in County Roscommon, in the western province of Connacht. Though tiny, the cave carries great mythic weight. It forms part of the Cruachan complex, the ancient capital of Connacht built around the fort of the queen Medb. Its small mouth, about three feet high and four feet wide, comes from a medieval souterrain and opens into a huge cathedral-like space. The cave was the birthplace of Medb. The fairy queen Étain stopped there while fleeing with her lover Midir from her human husband. Her maidservant Crochan gave her name to the land around it. Midir went to see a relative in the cave, the obscure Sinech. Delighted with the place, which served as a great palace of the Otherworld though it looked a dingy cave, Crochan begged to stay, and there her daughter Medb was born. The cave also appears in the adventure of Nera, who spared Cruachan from an otherworld attack. He met and married a fairy woman in the cave, and she warned that Medb's palace would burn on Samhain. So Medb and Ailill mac Máta came into the cave to end the danger.",
